{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792495734,"nonce":"pIm3jvSuoXhosXVcHEVCUG71AIg=","message":"Final-source native validation on Apple M1 Pro / Metal: all seven offscreen composite application GPU tests pass, along with the CPU scratch-fingerprint test, normally and with forced vertex storage off (VB) and both storage flags off (DT). The four existing motion application cases pass in all three modes too. Fallback capacities are 1024 for primitives/glyphs with BLINC_MULTISTOP_VERTEX=1. All temporary capability overrides are restored. Final logs: /private/tmp/blinc-composite-{normal,vb,dt}-app-{composite,motion}.log.\n\nThe final normal native regressions also pass: producer opacity2, ordered overlay7, auxiliary routing2, display-list33 and clip fill rule1, totaling45. New cases exercise scratch overlap and straight alpha, exact texture extents, nested path-only ranges, actual motion/CSS promotion walkers with cached 0/0.5/0.75/1 opacity updates and invariant scratch fingerprints, effect-only rebaking, primitive-local polygon-clipped meshes and restored screen-space state, a nested blur halo beyond the primitive footprint, and the scratch CSS full-repaint guard. The guard fixture injects scratch-owned CSS metadata; it is not a claim of mixed CSS in-place patching. Promotion fixtures invoke actual walker capture and live overlay methods, insert the texture into the same cache, and compare fingerprints; they do not drive an owner desktop window or the full window event loop.\n\nGroup ownership now uses a saved static/dynamic/composite batch key. Composite children omit only represented group alpha while retaining explicit or unrepresented ancestor factors. A Pop goes back to its original batch after routing changes. Composite scratch bounds reuse ordered nodes, including paths and effect margins, even while the promoted root's outer group remains open. Tight baking clears an exact pooled target, draws nested nodes in order, converts its premultiplied result to straight alpha for the existing live blit, then restores viewport uniforms and screen-space aux data. The scratch fingerprint covers path geometry/style, complete command snapshots, effects and 3D parameters. Motion records routed to scratch stay out of the dynamic patcher, and scratch-owned CSS records bail before static-cache mutation.\n\nLimits: this does not isolate a group spanning independent streams, foreground or late images, or add named LayerCommand::Sample support. Existing native effect expansion conventions remain unchanged. Browser WebGL2/mobile pixels, frame timings and memory benchmarks are unverified. The parent e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a remains open. No code or bug refs have been pushed.","files":null}]}